From db4fbca0e0b69af71b37869999dbfb908d28e816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The FBC Agent <thefbcspecialagent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:56:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] video: SDL2 framebuffer window on Windows too
 (XBOX_SDL_WINDOW)

fb_present_sdl.c moves from pthreads and __atomic builtins to SDL's lock,
atomics and timer, so it also builds with MSVC. With the new CMake option
XBOX_SDL_WINDOW (default OFF, Windows only) it replaces the GDI window
there: the window runs on its own "fb window" thread, opened by
xbox_FramebufferWindowStart as the GDI one is, and the guest stays where it
is; per-monitor DPI on that thread as before. POSIX keeps
xbox_HostWindowMain unchanged.

New in both hosts: xbox_FramebufferWindowExternalPresent(1), called before
the window opens by a renderer that draws into the window itself; the SDL
window then makes no SDL_Renderer (its swap chain would fight a GL context)
and drops CPU frames. Hwnd (Windows, SDL_GetWindowWMInfo) and ClientSize
(physical pixels, 0 while minimised) answer as the GDI window's. Alt+Enter
and RECOMP_FB_FULLSCREEN give SDL's desktop fullscreen. The GDI window
ignores the new call. A parent project may provide the SDL2::SDL2 target
(e.g. built static from source) before add_subdirectory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ahYm8JBvCH5KhgtSu9Yoy
